<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Prompts and tool definitions.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Each full agent receives a system prompt, the item as its user prompt, and four tool definitions through the API (Figure <a href="#A2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Prompts and tool definitions. ‣ Appendix B Prompts, Tool Results, and Conditions ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>); Grep adds a fifth, and the definitions are otherwise the same in every condition. Across conditions, the system prompt changes only in its <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> line (Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Prompts and tool definitions. ‣ Appendix B Prompts, Tool Results, and Conditions ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and in the mode named in its last line. The no-tool baselines send the item text alone with one of two system prompts (Figure <a href="#A2.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ Prompts and tool definitions. ‣ Appendix B Prompts, Tool Results, and Conditions ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F2" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A2.F2.2" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage" style="width:169.1pt;">
          
<div id="A2.F2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.F2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A2.F2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:162.3pt;">
<span id="A2.F2.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F2.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System prompt (full agents, TOC condition)
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A2.F2.p1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter"># Role
<br class="ltx_break">You are an expert geochemist and PHREEQC simulation specialist.
<br class="ltx_break">Your goal is to answer multiple-choice geochemistry questions (A/B/C/D) by writing and executing PHREEQC simulations.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;">
# Tools
<br class="ltx_break">- list_file(path): List files/directories in the workspace.
<br class="ltx_break">- read_file(path, start_line?, end_line?): Read a text file. Large files are auto-truncated; use start_line/end_line for specific sections.
<br class="ltx_break">- write_file(path, new_content): Create or overwrite a text file.
<br class="ltx_break">- execute_phreeqc(input_path): Run PHREEQC on an input file. Returns metadata and a TOC for result.out. File contents are NOT included — use read_file to inspect results.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;">
# Rules
<br class="ltx_break">- All file operations must use relative paths within the workspace.
<br class="ltx_break">- Do NOT include a DATABASE line in PHREEQC input files (the database is provided externally).
<br class="ltx_break">- A database reference (database_reference.txt) is available in your workspace listing valid species, minerals, gases, and built-in RATES blocks. Consult it before writing input files.
<br class="ltx_break">- Base your final answer on PHREEQC output, not memory. Do not guess.
<br class="ltx_break">- If your computed value does not match any option, your input is likely wrong — fix and re-run rather than picking the closest option.
<br class="ltx_break">- Call only one tool per turn.
<br class="ltx_break">- Write your final answer to final_answer.txt with exact content: &lt;&lt;&lt; X &gt;&gt;&gt; followed by a newline.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;">
# Context mode for this run
<br class="ltx_break">The execute_phreeqc tool is configured in `toc` mode. Use the payload it returns according to the tool contract above.
</span></span>
</span></p>
