<p id="A2.F2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A2.F2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:162.3pt;">
<span id="A2.F2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F2.p2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">User prompt (full agents)
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A2.F2.p2.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter">Answer the multiple-choice question below.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;">
Question:
<br class="ltx_break"></span><span id="A2.F2.p2.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_italic">[item text with options A–D]
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span><span id="A2.F2.p2.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter">
Use tools as needed for PHREEQC / quantitative work.
</span></span>
</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A2.F2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.F2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A2.F2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:162.3pt;">
<span id="A2.F2.p3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F2.p3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Tool definitions (API function schemas)
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A2.F2.p3.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter">write_file(path, new_content): Create or overwrite a text file in the workspace.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.0pt;">
read_file(path, start_line?, end_line?): Read a text file. Optionally specify start_line/end_line (1-based) for a range.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.0pt;">
list_file(path?): List files and directories in the workspace.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.0pt;">
execute_phreeqc(input_path): Run PHREEQC on an input file. Returns execution status, stdout/stderr, output file paths, and the result payload configured for this run’s context mode.
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:2.0pt;">
grep_file(path, pattern, max_matches?, context_lines?, case_sensitive?) </span><span id="A2.F2.p3.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_italic">[Grep only]</span><span id="A2.F2.p3.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter">: Search a text file line-by-line with a regular expression (case-insensitive by default). Returns matching line numbers with surrounding context lines. Use read_file with start_line/end_line to inspect a region around a match.
</span></span>
</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A2.F2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.F2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A2.F2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:162.3pt;">
<span id="A2.F2.p4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F2.p4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System prompt (Direct baseline)
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A2.F2.p4.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter">You are a geochemistry expert. Answer the multiple-choice question. Your entire response must be EXACTLY &lt;&lt;&lt; X &gt;&gt;&gt; where X is A, B, C, or D. No explanation, no reasoning, no other text. ONLY &lt;&lt;&lt; X &gt;&gt;&gt;.
</span></span>
</span></p>
</div>
          
<div id="A2.F2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.F2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A2.F2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:162.3pt;">
<span id="A2.F2.p5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F2.p5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">System prompt (CoT baseline)
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A2.F2.p5.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_typewriter">You are a geochemistry expert. Solve the multiple-choice question by reasoning step by step, but do not use tools. End your response with the final answer in the exact form &lt;&lt;&lt; X &gt;&gt;&gt;, where X is A, B, C, or D.
</span></span>
</span></p>
</div>
        
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 2: </span>Prompts and tool definitions, verbatim. Left: the system prompt of the full agents, shown for TOC; other conditions replace its <span id="A2.F2.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> line (Figure <a href="#A2.F3" title="Figure 3 ‣ Prompts and tool definitions. ‣ Appendix B Prompts, Tool Results, and Conditions ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>) and the mode name. Right: their user prompt; the tool definitions passed through the API, with parameters abridged (“?”: optional), the same in every condition except that <span id="A2.F2.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">grep_file</span> is offered only in Grep; and the system prompts of the no-tool baselines, whose user prompt is the item text alone.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure">
<p id="A2.F3.2" class="ltx_p">
<span id="A2.F3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_middle ltx_framed ltx_framed_rectangle" style="width:338.2pt;">
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">The <span id="A2.F3.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> line of the system prompt, by condition
<br class="ltx_break" style="--ltx-break-space:3.0pt;"></span>
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_font_bold">Raw100k:</span> “Run PHREEQC on an input file. Returns metadata and raw result.out content inline, truncated if very large. Use read_file only if you need to inspect an additional output file or re-read a specific portion.”</span>
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F3.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TOC:</span> “Run PHREEQC on an input file. Returns metadata and a TOC for result.out. File contents are NOT included — use read_file to inspect results.”</span>
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F3.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Grep:</span> “Run PHREEQC on an input file. Returns metadata only (status, output file paths and sizes, result.out line count). File contents are NOT included — locate evidence with grep_file, then read specific line ranges with read_file.” followed by “grep_file(path, pattern, max_matches?, context_lines?, case_sensitive?): Search a text file line-by-line with a regular expression (case-insensitive by default). Returns matching line numbers with a few lines of surrounding context. Use it to find sections, species, or numeric fields in result.out, then read_file with start_line/end_line to inspect the full region.” and “NOTE: In this mode, read_file on a large file WITHOUT start_line/end_line returns no content. Always grep_file first to find line numbers, then read the range you need.”</span>
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F3.2.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hybrid:</span> “Run PHREEQC on an input file. Returns metadata plus the raw result.out content inline when it is small enough. For a large result.out it returns a TOC instead (section names with starting line numbers) and no content; in that case use read_file with start_line/end_line to read the sections you need.”</span>
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F3.2.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TOC+Round:</span> the TOC line followed by “IMPORTANT: The answer options give each value at a fixed precision. If a value you read has more digits than the options, round it to the options’ precision to the nearest value; do not truncate digits. Choose the option that equals the correctly rounded value.”</span>
<span id="A2.F3.2.1.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.F3.2.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">TOC+Report:</span> the TOC line followed by “IMPORTANT: The authoritative values are in result.out, printed at the precision the answer options use. Before answering, read the section of result.out that contains the quantity you need and take the value exactly as printed there. Do not answer from SELECTED_OUTPUT or USER_PUNCH files: they print unrounded values that can match a neighboring option.”</span>
</span></p>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>The condition-specific <span id="A2.F3.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> line of the system prompt, verbatim. TOC+Report and TOC+Round also repeat their instruction in every tool result.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The inline description discourages additional reads, and the retrieval descriptions require them; part of the difference in reading behavior between inline and retrieval conditions may therefore be induced by the descriptions rather than by the return value alone; the paired replay, whose arms share one system prompt, still shows the loss (Appendix <a href="#A4" title="Appendix D Paired Replay with Computation Held Fixed ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">D</span></a>). The TOC+Report instruction both names the authoritative file and gives a reason to prefer it; TOC+Round gives only the rounding rule and names no file.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Tool results.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Every <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> call returns the exit status, the last 4,000 characters of PHREEQC’s standard output and error, and the names and sizes of the files the run created. Raw100k adds the report, cut to its first and last 50,000 characters with a truncation marker when it is longer than 100,000. TOC adds an index of the report’s dash-delimited section headers with their starting lines, at most 50 entries (the first and last 25 when a report has more), and the hint “Use read_file with start_line/end_line to read specific sections.” In the headline TOC runs and the TOC reruns the index was empty for reports longer than 100,000 characters, so on those items all four TOC runs use one separate run with the index built; all other runs build it for every report (Section <a href="#S2.SS2" title="2.2 Agents and Output Delivery ‣ 2 Setting ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2.2</span></a>). Hybrid adds the report when it fits and otherwise the index and the report length; Grep adds only the report’s line count. TOC+Report and TOC+Round return the TOC payload with their instruction appended to the hint, so the agent sees the instruction in the system prompt and again in every <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> result. With a line range, <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">read_file</span> returns the requested lines; without one it returns a file of up to 20,000 characters whole and otherwise its first and last 80 lines (no content in Grep).</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">An example trajectory.</h4>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A2.F4" title="Figure 4 ‣ An example trajectory. ‣ Appendix B Prompts, Tool Results, and Conditions ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> abridges a GPT-5.1 TOC trajectory on item 121, the item of Figure <a href="#S1.F1" title="Figure 1 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Same Simulation, Different Evidence: Where Retrieved Tool Output Costs LLM Agents Accuracy" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>. The agent defines a selected-output file in its first input, reads that file after the run, and answers with the truncation of the value it prints. It never opens <span id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">result.out</span>, although the index points to the section that prints the keyed value.</p>
