<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Trajectories.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze every full-agent run with complete logs on the 158 verified items: the three TOC reruns per model for Sonnet, GPT-5.4, GPT-5.2, and GPT-5.1 (items whose report exceeds 100k characters come from the run with the fixed index, as in the headline numbers), the logged inline and Grep runs, the Hybrid, TOC+Report, TOC+Round, and TOC control runs, the GPT-5.4 TOC+Report and logged inline runs, the Opus run with the fixed index (33 items), and the Gemini 3 Flash runs. This gives 5,773 distinct trajectories. Each workspace was matched to its item through the question text in the log.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Produced and seen.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For every <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">execute_phreeqc</span> call we rebuilt the input from the agent’s preceding <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">write_file</span> events and re-ran it with the same PHREEQC 3.8.6 binary and database (11,007 calls, 10,605 distinct inputs). The <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">produced</em> corpus is every output of these executions; the <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">seen</em> corpus is every tool result the agent received that carries simulator output (inline payloads, <span id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">read_file</span> results on the report or selected-output files, and search matches). A keyed value counts as present if a printed number equals the option at its precision, or rounds to it when printed with more digits; numbers on a rounding midpoint match both neighbors; for quantities described as dissolved, precipitated, or changed, the sign is ignored; specific-conductance options match only on conductance lines; the echo of the input in the report is excluded. A trajectory is labeled <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.6" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">build</em> if the keyed value was never produced, <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.7" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exposure</em> if it was produced but never seen, and <em id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.8" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">closure</em> if it was seen but the answer was wrong; trajectories without a gradable answer and wrong answers on non-numeric items are counted separately.</p>
</div>
